{
  "transcriptVersion": 1,
  "id": "locker-redirect-web",
  "description": "A web app signs a person in with the customer host on (plans/LK-00.md §3, §7.8): the same conversation as redirect-web-happy, but authorize answers 303 to https://polaris.locker/signin?request=rq_…&bind=<token> and sets no cookie. The customer host redeems the bind token once, sets the request's binder itself and answers 303 to /signin?request=rq_…; the card's Continue then runs on the customer host. Issuer, authorize and token stay on the API host, so the SDK's own request is the twin's token exchange. The bind URL carries no state, challenge or redirect URI, and a second visit to it is refused.",
